  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_037: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieves 0.706 acc. We know avgpool > transformer for pca_n2000 (0.591 vs 0.519), but that comparison used a weaker, linearly-reduced encoder. With scvi_n200's richer learned latent representations, transformer-based attention aggregation could better capture inter-profile interactions that simple averaging discards. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool when paired with the strongest RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and image encoder (imagenet_vit_l)? Why this experiment: It is a clean single-variable extension of the best-performing configuration (only aggregation changes), directly resolving whether the aggregation choice that was suboptimal for PCA might be optimal for learned embeddings. A positive result would open a new optimization direction; a negative result would confirm avgpool as the correct choice and let us focus remaining budget on other dimensions (e.g., fusion strategy or RNA encoder alternatives). This is the highest-information experiment available under the limited budget."
